### EPISTEMIC ARTICULACY

### Epistemic Instrumental Binding — Linguistic Implementation Cheat Sheet

Register: EIB–HI/ME/LO–001 Classification: Applied Linguistics · Epistemic Governance · Knowledge Acquisition · Information Integrity · Documentary Traceability

Purpose: Establish a practical linguistic instrument for receiving, classifying, interpreting, validating, and releasing incoming knowledge without compromising its original meaning, evidentiary status, or informational integrity.

Governing principle:

Incoming knowledge must be preserved before it is interpreted, interpreted before it is classified, and verified before it is represented as established fact.

### §1.0 — Incoming Knowledge: Acquisition & Preservation

| Instrument         | Linguistic operation            | Implementation                               |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Observation        | Identify incoming information   | Record what was actually communicated.       |
| Transcription      | Preserve original wording       | Retain the source statement.                 |
| Orthography        | Validate written representation | Examine spelling and word boundaries.        |
| Phonetics          | Examine speech characteristics  | Identify relevant speech sounds.             |
| Morphology         | Decompose word structure        | Identify roots, prefixes, and suffixes.      |
| Etymology          | Establish historical origins    | Examine lexical provenance.                  |
| Lexicology         | Classify vocabulary             | Identify technical and ordinary terminology. |
| Semantics          | Establish meaning               | Determine what the statement communicates.   |
| Syntax             | Examine grammatical structure   | Identify relationships between words.        |
| Pragmatics         | Examine contextual meaning      | Determine intended communicative function.   |
| Discourse Analysis | Examine broader communication   | Identify relationships across statements.    |
| Provenance         | Preserve source history         | Record origin, date, and transformations.    |

Integrity rule: Never silently replace the original statement with a corrected interpretation.

