### §3.0 — Incoming Knowledge Classification

Every incoming statement should be assigned an epistemic classification before institutional interpretation.

| Code | Classification     | Description                                         |
| ---- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |
| OBS  | Observation        | Directly recorded information                       |
| CLM  | Claim              | An assertion requiring evaluation                   |
| EVD  | Evidence           | Information offered in support of a claim           |
| INF  | Inference          | Conclusion derived from available information       |
| HYP  | Hypothesis         | Proposed explanation requiring testing              |
| OPN  | Opinion            | Personal evaluation or judgment                     |
| INT  | Interpretation     | Explanation of meaning or significance              |
| REG  | Regulation         | Formal rule or administrative requirement           |
| LAW  | Legal authority    | Applicable legal provision or controlling authority |
| SCI  | Scientific finding | Result supported by scientific methodology          |
| UNC  | Uncertainty        | Information that remains unresolved                 |
| DIS  | Disputed finding   | Matter subject to substantive disagreement          |
| REC  | Recommendation     | Proposed action based on available analysis         |

Important: A claim is not automatically evidence. An interpretation is not automatically a finding. A disputed assertion must remain distinguishable from a verified observation.

